 "description": "CPython 3.13's JSON decoder where the C recursion budget runs out, through all three scripts (state-helpers review). With B the deepest container a call site accepts (teams_feedback.py 9996, capacity.py and engage_parse.py 9998) and n the level of the innermost open container: NaN/Infinity need n < B; a decode error built in C (raise_errmsg) is a JSONDecodeError only while n <= B - 4, else RecursionError (so engage_parse.py does not salvage it and capacity.py does not report it); 'Expecting value' and the 4300-digit int fail to be created at n = B (RecursionError whose last traceback line is the note 'Normalization failed: ...'); fraction and exponent digits of a float do not count as an over-long int. Each deep case has a control one level shallower. Documents are written by helpers_probe.py write-nested.",
